WEBVTT

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.200
Clark?

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.199
Anyone home, sweet home?

00:00:08.199 --> 00:00:13.810
Guess not.

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:22.500
Mrs. Kay wouldn't approve.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:38.549
Don't tell me clerk's ditched you too, hmm?

00:00:38.549 --> 00:00:40.549
I know.

00:00:40.549 --> 00:00:48.929
Smallville isn't the same without Smallville, isn't.

00:00:48.929 --> 00:00:52.929
So if he's still on his whirlwind walkabout, who's been feeding you, huh?

00:00:52.929 --> 00:01:03.530
Hey, beautiful?

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.530
Are you still at the office?

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:06.530
No, I know.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:11.530
Sitting behind the desk just isn't the same without those pretty brown eyes of yours.

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:13.530
Oh, glaring about me.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:15.530
Since you don't want to grab dinner tonight,

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:17.530
I spent the time switching out the news,

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:19.530
and you'll never guess what I found.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:23.530
If I do, would you take me off your speed down?

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:25.530
It's very funny.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.530
Your favorite freak's been at it again, and this time the story's mine.

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:31.530
Take it, sticky fingers. There are plenty of headlines to go around.

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:33.530
Oh my goodness.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:36.530
I never thought you'd be willing to share the blur.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:37.530
Lois?

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.530
We should celebrate.

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:41.530
Over coffee, your place or mine.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:43.530
Or neither. Besides, I'm not even.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:45.530
exactly being generous.

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:47.530
You know, the blur catches more bad guys before breakfast

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:49.530
than most cops do in a day.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:51.530
Well, that's the problem. He's not a cop.

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:53.530
He's a vigilante.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:56.530
Superpowers in a thing for the letter, S.

00:01:56.530 --> 00:02:01.780
Well, then he's done a super job cleaning up Metropolis.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:04.780
Thanks to him, the city can sleep at night.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.780
What if he screws up?

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:09.780
How do you hold him accountable? No one's even seen his face?

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.780
John, after everything the blur's done for the world,

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:12.780
how can you be such a cynic?

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:13.780
Well, apparently, I don't suffer.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:18.780
I don't suffer from the same soft-hearted hero worship.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:19.780
You do.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:20.780
At least I have a heart.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:22.780
You gotta lighten up, John.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:25.780
Spend a little less time on the dark side of the street.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:30.539
There's another side of the blur and I'm gonna expose it.

00:02:30.539 --> 00:07:31.430
Please, I can rise and shine to a better world, courtesy of the blur.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:49.060
Uh, Lois, why is Clark's dog welcoming me home?

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:51.060
Oh, I dropped by the farm yesterday,

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:53.060
and I found Shelby all alone with her Wheaties.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:55.060
I thought Clark secretly came back and didn't tell us.

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:57.060
didn't tell us.

00:07:57.060 --> 00:08:01.060
So you decided to call him out by dog-napping his furry friend?

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:03.060
Lois.

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:04.060
I'm sorry.

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:06.060
I'm the one that was on pooch patrol.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:08.060
Clark still isn't back yet.

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:10.730
I know.

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:14.730
I called Mrs. Kay and she said he's visiting cousins in Poughkeepsie.

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:16.730
I mean, how long can you stay in Poughkeepsie?

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:18.730
Sounds like someone misses him.

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:22.939
Please, I don't miss Clark.

00:08:22.939 --> 00:08:26.939
I just can't stand the new guy that's at his desk.

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:28.939
He is a textbook, Hero,

00:08:28.939 --> 00:08:32.940
hate her. Oh, come on. Who hates the blur?

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:34.940
Anyone who reads can see how great he is.

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:40.590
It looks like he really is spreading his wings, doesn't it?

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:42.590
Yeah, I just hope he's not.

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:44.590
Spreading himself too thin.

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:47.590
I mean, he sounds a little lonely. I can hear it in his voice.

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:49.590
His voice.

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.590
Did he call you again?

00:08:51.590 --> 00:09:00.259
Well, I am as one and only contact at the paper.

00:09:00.259 --> 00:09:02.259
So was work related, but...

00:09:02.259 --> 00:09:06.259
Not really. I mean, he calls when I'm at work and

00:09:06.259 --> 00:09:11.259
He relates things to me, but I think sometimes he just calls to chat.

00:09:11.259 --> 00:09:16.259
I think maybe I'm the only person in his life that he can really turn to.

00:09:16.259 --> 00:09:21.460
That's incredible.

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:22.460
I know, right?

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:27.860
Anyway, can we table this tell-all till later?

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:28.860
I have to get ready.

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:31.860
It's time to step back into the ring with a certain CEO.

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:32.860
Bye.

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:33.860
Bye.

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:46.820
Shelby? Shelby?

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:51.019
Shelby.

00:09:51.019 --> 00:10:07.320
Lois stopped by and found Shelby here alone with a dish full of food.

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:08.320
Now don't worry, I covered for you.

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:12.320
but you should know that you're now on her radar.

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:13.919
Thanks, I'll be more careful next to them.

00:10:13.919 --> 00:10:16.220
Dress like that?

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:18.720
Frick, what if I was Lois?

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:23.220
She would take one look at you and realize that Clark Kent is the blur.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:24.919
I told you, there is no Clark Kent.

00:10:24.919 --> 00:10:27.019
No disrespect to your Kryptonian calling,

00:10:27.019 --> 00:10:33.639
but coming back to feed the dog is about as human as it gets.

00:10:33.639 --> 00:10:37.299
Are you still reaching out to Lois as the blur?

00:10:37.299 --> 00:10:38.500
She told you?

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:39.600
You're supposed to be training with you.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.700
With Jorale, does he know you're still talking to her?

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:42.700
Jarrell doesn't need to know.

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:43.700
So you're lying to him.

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:47.700
You say you're turning your back on all your human attachments, Clark?

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:49.700
But apparently only when it suits you.

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:53.700
You're taking this all too personally, Chloe.

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:55.700
And I understand you're still anger about Jim.

00:10:55.700 --> 00:10:59.700
We both sacrificed a lot so that you could become the hero you're meant to be.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:01.700
Now quit backpedaling, Clark.

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:05.700
Commit to what you started before more people get hurt.

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:17.820
Oh, God, huh. Don't get around me, please.

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:20.820
Okay, cooler heads, people.

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:23.820
It's got a trum panel, you wait, type and cross the floor.

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:25.820
They want more film on his chest and arms.

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:27.820
Dr. Hamilton, and you are?

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:30.820
You're in a nightmare. Look at me.

00:11:30.820 --> 00:11:32.820
Okay, I'll rule it out.

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:38.179
All right, who did this to you? I don't know.

00:11:38.179 --> 00:11:39.179
I don't know.

00:11:39.179 --> 00:11:44.179
I, uh, I got hit by a truck, and when I woke up, this...

00:11:44.179 --> 00:11:48.179
Excuse me. What is it? What is all this?

00:11:48.179 --> 00:11:50.179
Initial assessment. Someone is surgically implanted.

00:11:50.179 --> 00:11:53.179
Someone is surgically implanted a bionic matrix in you.

00:11:53.179 --> 00:11:54.179
Oh, Jesus.

00:11:54.179 --> 00:11:57.179
It appears to be powered by a fragment of a meteorite.

00:11:57.179 --> 00:11:59.179
So you can take it out of me.

00:11:59.179 --> 00:12:00.179
Right?

00:12:00.179 --> 00:12:02.179
I'm afraid not.

00:12:02.179 --> 00:12:05.179
They removed your heart.

00:12:05.179 --> 00:12:07.179
No, no.

00:12:07.179 --> 00:12:09.179
This apparatus is the only thing keeping you alive.

00:12:09.179 --> 00:12:12.179
I can, I got it, no.

00:12:12.179 --> 00:12:14.179
Those empty levels are spiking.

00:12:14.179 --> 00:12:15.179
No, no.

00:12:15.179 --> 00:12:17.179
No, no.

00:12:17.179 --> 00:12:19.179
Set it out. No, no, Kevin.

00:12:19.179 --> 00:12:55.750
Seriously, what is it with you in physical violence?

00:12:55.750 --> 00:13:01.750
The last time you and I saw each other, things did get a little physical, didn't they?

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:03.750
And then what happened, Tess?

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:05.750
Inquiring minds want to know.

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:07.750
You don't remember.

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:11.750
A three-week concussion can do that to you, but I think...

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:13.750
That you bonged me on the head, and then...

00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:14.750
Held me somewhere.

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:16.750
Held you?

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:18.750
It's wishful thinking, Lane.

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:21.750
When I came to, you were already gone.

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:24.750
We never did get to finish what we started, though.

00:13:26.419 --> 00:13:28.419
A little rematch?

00:13:28.419 --> 00:13:31.419
I won't fight you, Tess.

00:13:31.419 --> 00:13:33.419
I just came to tell you that I'm not leaving the Daily Planet.

00:13:33.419 --> 00:13:35.419
You were never leaving, Lois.

00:13:35.419 --> 00:13:37.419
I fired you.

00:13:37.419 --> 00:13:38.419
Well, I'm not going to get into the hole.

00:13:38.419 --> 00:13:39.419
She said...

00:13:39.419 --> 00:13:42.419
She said thing with you.

00:13:42.419 --> 00:13:43.419
But...

00:13:43.419 --> 00:13:45.419
I do have friends at the Inc.

00:13:45.419 --> 00:13:49.419
and they would just love to run a story about Luther Corp's CEO

00:13:49.419 --> 00:13:52.419
and her plans to launch a hostile alien takeover of the world.

00:13:52.419 --> 00:13:59.379
