00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:15.220
I'll see you at the office.

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:23.429
Shouldn't you be in school?

00:14:23.429 --> 00:14:28.409
Just a little fire, huh?

00:14:28.409 --> 00:14:30.409
Stewart.

00:14:30.409 --> 00:14:32.409
What is it?

00:14:32.409 --> 00:14:35.409
Um, it's about your missing Coptonians here.

00:14:35.409 --> 00:14:38.409
I extrapolated a dozen potential destinations,

00:14:38.409 --> 00:14:56.580
and I think I know where their pit stopped in Metropolis.

00:14:56.580 --> 00:15:00.580
I understand it took Chloe years to get used to your entrances.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:02.580
I heard what happened on the police scanner.

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:03.580
Is it a meteor freak?

00:15:03.580 --> 00:15:06.580
No, the man that did this is something far more disturbing.

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:10.580
I'd loose to classify him as a cyborg, part man, part machine.

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:12.580
Someone built him. Against his will.

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:15.580
I've seen this before. Lex had similar projects.

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:18.860
Not like this.

00:15:18.860 --> 00:15:22.100
Clark, they took his heart.

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:27.100
heart, evidently to make room for his bionic body's new energy source,

00:15:27.100 --> 00:15:29.100
a meteorite fragment.

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:31.100
And the synthesis between meteorine

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:33.100
clearly increased his strength,

00:15:33.100 --> 00:15:35.100
but it also boosted his adrenaline,

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:36.100
intensifying his emotions.

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:39.100
I fear, the longer that rock powers his body,

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:41.100
the mortal poison his mind.

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:43.100
We have to do something to help him soon,

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:45.100
or he could turn homicidal.

00:15:45.100 --> 00:15:47.100
He already put one of my orderlies in a coma.

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:51.090
I mean to find him before it hurts anyone else.

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:53.090
He didn't give me his name, but he did

00:15:53.090 --> 00:15:55.090
He did leave this behind.

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:57.090
He must have dropped out of his pocket.

00:15:57.090 --> 00:16:02.200
These are given to every new employee at the Daily Planet.

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:04.200
He must work at the paper.

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:06.200
Well, then you won't be hard to find.

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:08.200
Green glow's hard to miss.

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:13.500
Emil, I need a favor.

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:23.299
Ah!

00:16:23.299 --> 00:16:24.299
Ha!

00:16:24.299 --> 00:16:28.299
Ha!

00:16:28.299 --> 00:16:33.460
Your favorite freaks been at it again.

00:16:33.460 --> 00:16:34.460
This time the story's mine.

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:39.460
Well, then, he's done a super job cleaning up Metropolis.

00:16:39.460 --> 00:16:42.480
What if he's really is working?

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:43.480
Crews out.

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:49.450
Next to him, the city can sleep behind.

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:58.019
This apparatus is the only thing keeping you alive.

00:16:58.019 --> 00:16:59.019
No, no.

00:16:59.019 --> 00:17:02.840
There's another side to the blur.

00:17:02.840 --> 00:17:04.839
I'm gonna expose it.

00:17:04.839 --> 00:17:05.839
Becca.

00:17:05.839 --> 00:17:41.400
This happened.

00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:44.400
Beka, I don't know who did it, but I know.

00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:49.400
Who did it, but I know.

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:54.700
Why?

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:55.700
It's a gift.

00:17:55.700 --> 00:18:00.900
It's a gift.

00:18:00.900 --> 00:18:02.900
I thought I just wanted to unmask

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:06.900
I think you are, but now I know what I've wanted to do.

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:08.900
All the long is...

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:10.900
He's killed him.

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:18.150
Oh, with my own two hands.

00:18:18.150 --> 00:18:35.710
I don't know how you did it, Lane, but HR just made it official.

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:38.710
Welcome back. Where's Corbin? I got an assignment for.

00:18:38.710 --> 00:18:42.710
I mean God's gift to journalism? Five bucks says he's out stalking the blur.

00:18:42.710 --> 00:18:45.710
Keep it for cab fare. I need you to head down the hospital.

00:18:45.710 --> 00:18:49.710
Cover his story. Patient went on a rampage, destroyed the ER.

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:51.710
You're giving me Corbin's left-up.

00:18:51.710 --> 00:19:00.910
Make a meal of it, Lane.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:03.910
Daily Planet, Lois Lane, your first choice in reporting.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:04.910
Lois.

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:06.910
I need some information.

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:10.339
It's you.

00:19:10.339 --> 00:19:13.339
Something just happened to Metropolis General in the ER.

00:19:13.339 --> 00:19:15.339
Oh yeah, I know all about it. I'm covering the story.

00:19:15.339 --> 00:19:16.339
Got any leads?

00:19:16.339 --> 00:19:18.339
Not yet.

00:19:18.339 --> 00:19:21.339
I don't know the man's identity, but I do have his keys.

00:19:21.339 --> 00:19:24.339
I think he works at the Daily Planet.

00:19:24.339 --> 00:19:26.339
He works here?

00:19:26.339 --> 00:19:30.339
Hey, do you want me to find out who's missing their keys?

00:19:30.339 --> 00:19:31.339
No.

00:19:31.339 --> 00:19:34.339
I'm just wondering if you may have noticed anyone.

00:19:34.339 --> 00:19:36.339
I am so on it.

00:19:36.339 --> 00:19:38.339
No, Lois, listen to me.

00:19:38.339 --> 00:19:40.339
This man is dangerous.

00:19:40.339 --> 00:19:45.339
He's some sort of superhuman cyborg, and I don't want you to get hurt.

00:19:45.339 --> 00:19:48.339
You really do care about me, don't you?

00:19:48.339 --> 00:19:50.339
Lois.

00:19:50.339 --> 00:19:54.339
Okay, okay. I'll just keep my eyes open, I swear.

00:19:54.339 --> 00:19:58.339
But if I do see anything, it's not like I can call you from the bullpen.

00:19:58.339 --> 00:20:00.339
Then I'll call you at our phone booth.

00:20:00.339 --> 00:20:03.339
You think of it as our phone booth, too?

00:20:03.339 --> 00:20:06.339
Just be there at seven.

00:20:06.339 --> 00:20:23.269
I need to get into the archive room, but forget the lowest forgot her keys.

00:20:23.269 --> 00:20:24.269
Can I bar yours?

00:20:24.269 --> 00:20:28.900
Make sure you return him, Lane.

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:30.900
I just remembered where I stashed mine.

00:20:30.900 --> 00:20:35.339
Hi, I'm doing a special interest piece.

00:20:35.339 --> 00:20:38.339
They say you can tell a lot about a person from their keys.

00:20:38.339 --> 00:20:39.339
May I?

00:20:39.339 --> 00:20:43.950
Is that a foot?

00:20:43.950 --> 00:20:44.950
For a look.

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:49.259
Superstitious and disgusting.

00:20:49.259 --> 00:21:03.509
Chloe?

00:21:03.509 --> 00:21:04.509
Hello!

00:21:04.509 --> 00:21:06.509
I was just checking my email.

00:21:06.509 --> 00:21:09.509
You know, when I asked if we could table our talk about you know who,

00:21:09.509 --> 00:21:11.509
I met until I got home.

00:21:11.509 --> 00:21:15.509
Actually, the only table I'm here about is the kind they serve lunch on.

00:21:15.509 --> 00:21:18.509
I was thinking maybe we could celebrate you getting your job back.

00:21:18.509 --> 00:21:21.509
I would love to, but I'm kind of already on a job.

00:21:21.509 --> 00:21:24.509
I'm working for you know who.

00:21:24.509 --> 00:21:25.509
Blur?

00:21:25.509 --> 00:21:27.509
Mm-hmm. Doing what exactly?

00:21:27.509 --> 00:21:29.509
Hunting down a real-life Terminator.

00:21:29.509 --> 00:21:31.509
Lois, that sounds dangerous.

00:21:31.509 --> 00:21:33.509
Why is he not doing that himself?

00:21:33.509 --> 00:21:36.509
Sometimes heroes can't do it all on their own, Chloe.

00:21:36.509 --> 00:21:38.509
That's why they need sidekicks.

00:21:38.509 --> 00:21:46.180
Rain check on lunch.

00:21:46.180 --> 00:21:49.180
These were all stolen from different Luther Corps facilities over the last week.

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:52.180
Your visitors managed to hack into the lower-end alarm system.

00:21:52.180 --> 00:21:53.180
Shocker.

00:21:53.180 --> 00:21:55.180
Security didn't notice anything was gone until this morning,

00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:59.549
but I tracked the container's GPS.

00:21:59.549 --> 00:22:02.549
This technology was meant for several unrelated projects.

00:22:02.549 --> 00:22:08.900
What were they building?

00:22:08.900 --> 00:22:13.759
Maybe Frankenstein's monster.

00:22:13.759 --> 00:22:15.759
I scaled a few of the firewalls over at MetGen, and I filled some pretty.

00:22:15.759 --> 00:22:17.759
Jen and it feels pretty sick x-rays.

00:22:17.759 --> 00:22:24.089
Not exactly your basic bypass surgery.

00:22:24.089 --> 00:22:27.089
Luther Corp has the best scientist on Earth,

00:22:27.089 --> 00:22:34.380
and none ever thought to put these pieces together.

00:22:34.380 --> 00:22:38.380
It's impossible to put this much turbocharged hardware into one person.

00:22:38.380 --> 00:22:41.380
The equipment alone requires a massive power source.

00:22:41.380 --> 00:22:44.380
Why do you give someone such a major power up and then just let him go?

00:22:44.380 --> 00:23:01.460
Maybe it was a test, and to see if it would work.

00:23:01.460 --> 00:23:05.420
They could still be monitoring him.

00:23:05.420 --> 00:23:10.549
Zad and his people are one step closer to go.

00:23:10.549 --> 00:23:12.549
step closer to getting their powers.

00:23:12.549 --> 00:23:24.940
Well, it looks like the night shift finally clocked in.

00:23:24.940 --> 00:23:27.940
What happened? Try to shave in your sleep?

00:23:27.940 --> 00:23:30.940
What are the electronic records in this place only go back a year?

00:23:30.940 --> 00:23:33.940
Hello, Lois.

00:23:33.940 --> 00:23:37.940
Banter, banter, banter. What happened? Did your snappy patter set the sun?

00:23:37.940 --> 00:23:39.940
Where are the records?

00:23:39.940 --> 00:23:45.400
A little less snap and a little more patter, please.

00:23:45.400 --> 00:23:49.400
Okay, it's a new system. They haven't transferred it all over yet.

00:23:49.400 --> 00:23:51.400
There's a hard copy of everything in the sun.

00:23:51.400 --> 00:23:52.400
the archive room.

00:23:52.400 --> 00:23:53.400
What are you looking for?

00:23:53.400 --> 00:23:56.029
The blur?

00:23:56.029 --> 00:23:59.539
He can't come out of nowhere, Lowe.

00:23:59.539 --> 00:24:02.539
There must be some kind of boring story.

00:24:02.539 --> 00:24:06.140
Maintenance crew's already been through there.

00:24:06.140 --> 00:24:11.140
Don't forget your keys.

00:24:11.140 --> 00:24:12.140
I need to borrow yours.

00:24:12.140 --> 00:24:17.470
You don't have your keys?

00:24:17.470 --> 00:24:23.109
I must have lost mine.

00:24:23.109 --> 00:24:29.019
Keep them.

00:24:29.019 --> 00:24:31.019
I'll get them in the morning. It's late.

00:24:31.019 --> 00:24:49.730
I should go.

00:24:49.730 --> 00:24:50.730
Hello.

00:24:50.730 --> 00:24:51.730
It's me.

00:24:51.730 --> 00:24:54.730
Look, I know who he is.

00:24:54.730 --> 00:24:55.730
The man from the hospital, his name is John.

00:24:55.730 --> 00:24:57.730
his name is John Corbin.

00:24:57.730 --> 00:24:59.730
Lois, I ask you not to.

00:24:59.730 --> 00:25:00.730
Please be careful.

00:25:00.730 --> 00:25:02.730
Corbyn has a supersized grudge against you.

00:25:02.730 --> 00:25:04.730
And if he's as powerful as you say he is...

00:25:04.730 --> 00:25:05.730
I'll be fine.

00:25:05.730 --> 00:25:08.730
Just promise me that you're headed home and not back to the office.

00:25:08.730 --> 00:25:11.230
Lois.

00:25:11.230 --> 00:25:14.630
Lois.

00:25:14.630 --> 00:25:15.630
Lois!

00:25:15.630 --> 00:25:16.630
Lois!

00:25:16.630 --> 00:25:25.769
Corbent.

00:25:25.769 --> 00:25:41.779
Chloe, Lois has been kidnapped.

00:25:41.779 --> 00:25:43.779
I need your help.

00:25:43.779 --> 00:25:47.779
Tell me this isn't because you let her chase down that sinister cyborg all by herself.

00:25:47.779 --> 00:25:48.779
I told her not to get involved.

00:25:48.779 --> 00:25:49.779
Clark.

00:25:49.779 --> 00:25:50.779
What did you think?

00:25:50.779 --> 00:25:52.779
she was going to do. This is Lois.

00:25:52.779 --> 00:25:56.779
You know, she was just referring to herself as the Blur's sidekick.

00:25:56.779 --> 00:25:59.779
I should have never called her in the first place, but I can't let anything happen to her now.

00:25:59.779 --> 00:26:02.779
Well, Dr. Emile told me about this guy, and he said he has a kryptonite heart.

00:26:02.779 --> 00:26:05.779
Okay? You're not going to be able to get close enough to him to do anything about it.

00:26:05.779 --> 00:26:07.779
Give me this.

00:26:07.779 --> 00:26:13.779
This is an EMP grenade. It'll blast an electromagnetic pulse and stop any electronic device within 50 yards.

00:26:13.779 --> 00:26:17.779
I'm hoping it'll stop him long enough for me to get Lois to safety.

00:26:17.779 --> 00:26:19.779
Will it work against Meteor Rock?

00:26:19.779 --> 00:26:22.779
It's a chance I'm willing to take.

00:26:22.779 --> 00:26:25.779
The guy's name is John Corbin and who works at the Daily Planet.

00:26:25.779 --> 00:26:28.779
I haven't been able to find him anywhere.

00:26:28.779 --> 00:26:30.779
Clark, I wish she would come to me with this.

00:26:30.779 --> 00:26:33.779
Lois doesn't have any experience dealing with these things.

00:26:33.779 --> 00:26:35.779
Things have been easy with Lois lately.

00:26:35.779 --> 00:26:39.259
Talking to her just felt right.

00:26:39.259 --> 00:26:52.380
It's, uh, it's funny, you know.

00:26:52.380 --> 00:26:55.380
I always thought it sounded ridiculous when people said it, but

00:26:55.380 --> 00:26:57.380
it's kind of like having a piece of home.

00:26:57.380 --> 00:26:59.380
So the DVDs and the notes that you sent me?

00:26:59.380 --> 00:27:00.380
Awesome.

00:27:00.380 --> 00:27:04.380
Um, I miss you.

00:27:04.380 --> 00:27:07.380
Oh, and you better be practicing a foosball also

00:27:07.380 --> 00:27:10.380
because I'm taking my title as soon as I get back there, all right?

00:27:10.380 --> 00:27:17.430
Do me a favor, okay?

00:27:17.430 --> 00:27:18.430
Just be safe.

00:27:18.430 --> 00:27:20.430
Be careful in the city, all right?

00:27:20.430 --> 00:27:22.430
It's not like home.

00:27:22.430 --> 00:27:23.430
All right?

00:27:23.430 --> 00:27:27.309
I love you.

00:27:27.309 --> 00:27:37.720
Bye.

00:27:37.720 --> 00:27:39.720
It's his sister, Rebecca Corbin.

00:27:39.720 --> 00:27:43.720
She was murdered in her apartment in Metropolis three months ago while he was overseas.

00:27:43.720 --> 00:27:45.720
Wait a minute.

00:27:45.720 --> 00:27:46.720
He bought the building just a few of you.

00:27:46.720 --> 00:27:48.720
the building just a few weeks ago.

00:27:48.720 --> 00:27:52.000
Maybe that's where he took Lois.

00:27:52.000 --> 00:27:54.000
Thanks, Chloe.

00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:55.000
Wait, Clerk.

00:27:55.000 --> 00:27:56.000
Be careful.

00:27:56.000 --> 00:28:11.420
Look, I know you're new at the planet John,

00:28:11.420 --> 00:28:14.420
but I'm pretty sure HR frowns on this kind of thing.

00:28:14.420 --> 00:28:17.420
I heard you.

00:28:17.420 --> 00:28:19.420
Lois, I heard you talking to him.

00:28:19.420 --> 00:28:21.420
So you're the blur is.

00:28:21.420 --> 00:28:24.420
And I'll let you go. I promise, I'll let you go.

00:28:24.420 --> 00:28:25.420
I'll let you go.

00:28:25.420 --> 00:28:27.420
I already told you. I don't know.

00:28:27.420 --> 00:28:32.420
Since when did you become a living light bright?

00:28:32.420 --> 00:28:41.140
What happened to you, John?

00:28:41.140 --> 00:28:42.140
Huh?

00:28:42.140 --> 00:28:54.180
I'll show you.

00:28:54.180 --> 00:28:59.819
Okay, take it easy there, Chippendale.

00:28:59.819 --> 00:29:01.819
I think I want to ship back on.

00:29:01.819 --> 00:29:25.650
I don't know.

00:29:25.650 --> 00:29:26.650
Get away from her!

00:29:26.650 --> 00:29:50.720
The blur.

00:29:50.720 --> 00:29:52.720
I don't want to hurt you, John.

00:29:52.720 --> 00:29:55.720
You already have.

00:29:55.720 --> 00:29:59.190
My sister's dead because of you.

00:29:59.190 --> 00:30:04.519
A prison bus.

00:30:04.519 --> 00:30:06.519
Crashed.

00:30:06.519 --> 00:30:07.519
Women inside would have died.

00:30:07.519 --> 00:30:09.519
and inside would have died, but you saved them all.

00:30:09.519 --> 00:30:12.519
And in the confusion, a cold-blooded killer escaped.

00:30:12.519 --> 00:30:17.400
And he murdered your sister.

00:30:17.400 --> 00:30:24.190
What gives you the right to interfere with our lives

00:30:24.190 --> 00:30:27.190
and to change our faith?

00:30:27.190 --> 00:30:33.609
I'm sorry about your loss, John.

00:30:33.609 --> 00:30:37.180
What happened to your sister was tragic.

00:30:37.180 --> 00:30:38.180
You need to control yourself.

00:30:38.180 --> 00:30:41.180
The meteor rock is causing an adrenaline rush.

00:30:41.180 --> 00:30:42.180
You're not thinking straight.

00:30:42.180 --> 00:30:45.180
Control myself.

00:30:45.180 --> 00:30:47.180
That's easy for you to say.

00:30:47.180 --> 00:30:52.180
It doesn't take much to stay in control

00:30:52.180 --> 00:30:54.180
when you watch from the shadows.

00:30:54.180 --> 00:30:59.859
You stand apart from the world.

00:30:59.859 --> 00:31:01.859
Well, the rest of us live in it.

00:31:01.859 --> 00:31:05.529
Even when it breaks your heart,

00:31:05.529 --> 00:32:36.710
it feels like to lose somebody you love.

00:32:36.710 --> 00:33:11.839
The meteor rock got you down?

00:33:11.839 --> 00:33:15.839
Who knew the mighty Goliath could be taken down

00:33:15.839 --> 00:33:17.839
with a simple stone?

00:33:17.839 --> 00:33:19.839
John?

00:33:19.839 --> 00:33:55.339
You're safe now, Los.

00:33:55.339 --> 00:33:56.339
I'm here.

00:33:56.339 --> 00:34:23.389
It's you.

00:34:23.389 --> 00:34:26.730
Save me.

00:34:26.730 --> 00:34:34.579
After all our phone calls, I finally have you standing right in front of me, and I don't know what to say to you.

00:34:34.579 --> 00:34:44.940
Please let me see your face.

00:34:44.940 --> 00:35:15.739
Lois, I'm just glad you're okay.

00:35:15.739 --> 00:35:17.739
I'm coming home right now.

00:35:17.739 --> 00:35:20.739
Okay. I'll see you soon.

00:35:20.739 --> 00:35:31.829
This view really puts things in perspective.

00:35:31.829 --> 00:35:37.780
Jimmy knew exactly what he was doing when he bought this place.

00:35:37.780 --> 00:35:48.500
I really miss him.

00:35:48.500 --> 00:35:59.659
I took the easy way out, Chloe.

00:35:59.659 --> 00:36:04.670
I should have been there when you needed me.

00:36:04.670 --> 00:36:07.019
I'm sorry.

00:36:07.019 --> 00:36:18.469
Clark, there's nothing easy about burying everyone you love in your past.

00:36:18.469 --> 00:36:25.309
I'm afraid I haven't even done a very good job of that.

00:36:25.309 --> 00:36:33.039
I've been trying to fill the void by hanging out on rooftops, eavesdropping on people.

00:36:33.039 --> 00:36:37.039
People are connecting and living.

00:36:37.039 --> 00:36:42.309
Thinking what's the point of protecting life?

00:36:42.309 --> 00:36:45.309
If you've lost your sense on how to live it.

00:36:45.309 --> 00:36:51.730
Maybe I can't do this, Chloe.

00:36:51.730 --> 00:36:55.730
Maybe I can't completely stay away.

00:36:55.730 --> 00:37:06.579
Stay away from her, you mean.

00:37:06.579 --> 00:37:13.699
Lois means something to you, something more.

00:37:13.699 --> 00:37:16.699
So does this mean that Clark Kent is coming back for an encore?

00:37:16.699 --> 00:37:23.929
But I can't let that life interfere with my training again.

00:37:23.929 --> 00:37:29.929
Clark, lurking around building edges at midnight, pining after the life you gave up,

00:37:29.929 --> 00:37:33.929
isn't exactly amping your hero performance either.

00:37:33.929 --> 00:37:48.409
You know, maybe I was naive to think that you could just turn a corner and never look back.

00:37:48.409 --> 00:37:49.409
But either way, Caliard,

00:37:49.409 --> 00:37:51.409
needs his human disguise now more than ever.

00:37:51.409 --> 00:37:53.409
Why do you say that?

00:37:53.409 --> 00:37:56.409
To the daily planet to look at Lois' computer

00:37:56.409 --> 00:38:00.409
and found that Tess had loaded it up with serious spyware.

00:38:00.409 --> 00:38:02.409
You mean she didn't rehire Lois out of the goodness of her heart?

00:38:02.409 --> 00:38:05.409
No, she wanted to find out where Lois has been the last three weeks.

00:38:05.409 --> 00:38:07.409
Now, if she figures out that...

00:38:07.409 --> 00:38:10.409
She was in the future, and brought back a Kryptonian who says I'll end the world.

00:38:10.409 --> 00:38:13.409
Tess already knows way too much about you.

00:38:13.409 --> 00:38:16.409
We can't let her get to Lois' memories before you do.

00:38:16.409 --> 00:38:41.639
Heartless bastard.

00:38:41.639 --> 00:39:04.780
I'm going to be needed.

00:39:04.780 --> 00:39:07.800
that.

00:39:07.800 --> 00:39:11.179
Clark, kid, you're back.

00:39:11.179 --> 00:39:14.179
I was beginning to think your family lived on some distant planet.

00:39:14.179 --> 00:39:21.139
Musta really missed me.

00:39:21.139 --> 00:39:25.139
Only because the guy who sat in your desk was a certifiable psychopath.

00:39:25.139 --> 00:39:31.530
Otherwise, I've been so busy, I didn't even notice you were gone.

00:39:31.530 --> 00:39:38.550
Missed you, too, Lois.

00:39:38.550 --> 00:39:43.460
Anything exciting happened while I was gone?

00:39:43.460 --> 00:39:45.460
Well, you'll never believe it.

00:39:45.460 --> 00:39:48.460
But I helped the blur stop a homic

00:39:48.460 --> 00:39:50.460
Really?

00:39:50.460 --> 00:39:55.289
You know, I would love to hear about it.

00:39:55.289 --> 00:39:56.289
Okay.

00:39:56.289 --> 00:40:05.739
It all started when this guy showed up with this major rug against the blur.

00:40:05.739 --> 00:40:10.739
He also happens to have these bionic arms and a big glowing rock for a heart.

00:40:10.739 --> 00:40:12.739
But that's way later on in the story.

00:40:12.739 --> 00:40:22.090
To think such a small rock could give someone so much power.

00:40:22.090 --> 00:40:24.090
Can he be revived?

00:40:24.090 --> 00:40:28.090
The subject's operation has left him more machine than man.

00:40:28.090 --> 00:40:31.090
His vital signs have simply gone offline.

00:40:31.090 --> 00:40:36.579
You have the coolest stuff.

00:40:36.579 --> 00:40:38.579
What?

00:40:38.579 --> 00:40:39.579
Hey.

00:40:39.579 --> 00:40:40.579
What?

00:40:40.579 --> 00:40:43.579
You work for me now, which means you knock before you enter.

00:40:43.579 --> 00:40:48.500
Did you find the Candorians?

00:40:48.500 --> 00:40:51.500
Check it.

00:40:51.500 --> 00:40:53.500
Look.

00:40:53.500 --> 00:40:57.500
These symbols appeared all over the world the same night that Zod arrived.

00:40:57.500 --> 00:40:59.500
Now, I don't have a definitive translation for them yet,

00:40:59.500 --> 00:41:04.500
but the design shares similarities to quotidian words

00:41:04.500 --> 00:41:07.500
for blood, nobility, and a family.

00:41:07.500 --> 00:41:11.469
Like a family crest.

00:41:11.469 --> 00:41:12.469
Crest.

00:41:12.469 --> 00:41:14.469
So there are more of his people out there.

00:41:14.469 --> 00:41:16.469
But how many of these did you find?

00:41:16.469 --> 00:41:17.469
Hundreds.

00:41:17.469 --> 00:41:18.469
Okay?

00:41:18.469 --> 00:41:21.469
And I think you might recognize this one.

00:41:21.469 --> 00:41:27.599
But there's more look.

